Native authorship and provenance
--------------------------------
Agent Memory is a reference architecture for governed memory in autonomous and agentic systems.

Proportional Adaptive Mutation Authority (PAMA), including the Agent Memory framing of M0-M5 mutation target classes, lifecycle strength, requested operations, A0-A5 downstream authority, and consequence-proportional mutation governance, is native Agent Memory doctrine authored by Kevin R. Knapp.

The thermodynamic-ground-state framing used in the cited UOR thermodynamic memory-lifecycle proposal is also recorded in this repository as a Kevin R. Knapp contribution. Public hosting or citation location does not change that provenance statement.

